{"parentUuid":"ea7fe99b-9372-44fc-b5b4-87b2260dfeb8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9bdfc07b-8ff1-4e95-9c88-de7440fd6192","agentId":"a0c5ef395232695eb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ao6rzVzYEmoch4TdCwvZhP","type":"tool_result","content":"   \"owner\": \"ai-assisted-authoring\",\n   \"evidence\": \"Unity AI; Roblox Assistant\",\n   \"revisit\": \"Licensing/provenance clear for training data\",\n   \"fallback\": \"Manual authoring\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"tech\": \"Agent/automation control API (MCP class)\",\n   \"class\": \"M\",\n   \"capabilities\": [\n    \"ED.ARCH.agent-api\",\n    \"QA.FUNC.agent-exploration\"\n   ],\n   \"owner\": \"editor-architect\",\n   \"evidence\": \"MCP integrations for major engines (2025); EA SEED RL testing\",\n   \"revisit\": \"Stable protocol adoption\",\n   \"fallback\": \"CLI/commandlets\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"tech\": \"GPU & training cook steps\",\n   \"class\": \"M\",\n   \"capabilities\": [\nL01 | Central sequential update loop\nL02 | Per-object virtual Tick()\nL03 | Game-thread / render-thread dichotomy\nL04 | Main-thread-only engine APIs\nL05 | Pervasive inheritance object hierarchies\nL06 | Possession / controller-pawn model by habit\nL07 | Universal scene graph\nL08 | Hidden globals & singletons\nL09 | Process-global mutable cvars read anywhere\nL10 | Hot-path virtual dispatch across contracts\nL11 | Coarse locks & global renderer sync\nL12 | Draw-call-centric CPU submission on capable tiers\nL13 | DX11/OpenGL binding & sync assumptions\nL14 | Per-object render proxy mirror\nL15 | Frame-tied resource lifetimes\nL16 | Synchronous IO / blocking loads\nL17 | Page-fault-driven streaming\nL18 | Level-as-a-file loading\nL19 | Immediate synchronous observer callbacks across subsystems\nL20 | Stringly-typed reflection on runtime paths\nL21 | Tracing-GC-managed engine objects\nL22 | Global script VM on one thread\nL23 | Editor-in-runtime monolith\nL24 | Blocking cook-before-play\nL25 | Single-thread-first design\nL26 | Monolithic subsystems\nL27 | ECS for everything / GPU-driven everywhere (new dogma)\ndata/contracts.json:675:   \"summary\": \"Required test kinds per skill, test determinism, coverage & mutation thresholds, the evidence bundle an implementer hands to S3/S4 critics, oracle independence, conformance suites owned by contract owners with consumer-driven additions.\",\ndata/critics.json:20:    \"no hidden cyclic build dependencies\",\ndata/critics.json:247:    \"no hidden global sync points\",\ndata/critics.json:379:    \"evidence bundle defined for S3/S4\"\ndata/legacy-patterns.json:55:   \"pattern\": \"Hidden globals & singletons\",\ndata/capabilities.json:1143:       \"Service registry & dependency-injection policy (no hidden globals)\",\ndocs/09-radar-legacy-milestones.md:78:| L08 | Hidden globals & singletons | static instances initialized implicitly | Service registry + init graph | core-runtime-architect |\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:97:| No hidden globals: services and self-registration run through an init graph, and config is read through immutable snapshots. | Implicitly initialized singletons; global cvars read from any thread. | These are required for parallel boot, testability and small configurations. |\ndocs/02-skill-dependency-graph.md:261:| `C-TEST` Test & validation definition of done | P | test-architect | — | universal (all) | Required test kinds per skill, test determinism, coverage & mutation thresholds, the evidence bundle an implementer hands to S3/S4 critics, oracle independence, conformance suites owned by contract owners with consumer-driven additions. |\ndocs/05-critic-framework.md:24:- Checks: every capability has exactly one owner and the owner is the right expertise; non-responsibilities point to the real owner; contracts are minimal, stable and layered; no hidden cyclic build dependencies; leads have real territory, not just coordination","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"b98205fd-fd2c-48e3-9e16-2c35b298cdc7","timestamp":"2026-09-29T16:25:40.805Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ea7fe99b-9372-44fc-b5b4-87b2260dfeb8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
